# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed: salman gates on bit-identical output across
# machines, and that is only meaningful with a locked dependency graph.
# (Do not add Cargo.lock here.)

# Fuzzing.
#
# fuzz/seeds/ is committed: a small, hand-written, meaningfully-named corpus
# that says what a target is meant to explore. fuzz/corpus/ is NOT: libFuzzer
# grows it by thousands of machine-named files per session, and committing that
# turns every fuzzing run into a repository the size of a small operating
# system. CI caches the grown corpus between runs instead.
fuzz/target/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage/
fuzz/corpus/

# Local scratch
/scratch/
*.local.toml

# IDE. Editor configuration is a personal choice, not a property of the project.
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
.vscode/
.fleet/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Scratch files a review agent leaves in a crate's tests/ directory while it is
# working. They are named so they sort last and so this pattern can catch them:
# one was committed by a `git add -A` mid-review, which is how this line came to
# exist.
crates/*/tests/zz_*.rs
